APPROVED asto form only:
By Stefanie Bo ster at8:37amov07223
RESOLUTION NO.
NECESSARY DOCUMENTS RELATED TO THE TRANS ER, PURCHASE
AND SALE OF A SPECIFIED PORTION OF THE PROPERTY LOCATED
AT503WEST COLLEGE DRIVE."
WHEREAS, as a result of the 2021November election and through the use of the voluntary
one percent (1%) specific purpose sales and use tax, voters in Laramie County approved the use
of taxpayer fundsfor the relocation and replacement of three(3)fire stations;
WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne wishes to build additional fire stations as needs demand.
Response times indicate that a fire station would be beneficial in south Cheyenne off of College
Drive;
WHEREAS, Steven and Carol Powers currently own property located at503West College
Drive and are willing to seli this property to the City of Cheyenne;
WHEREAS, during the November election and through the use of the voluntary one
percent (1%) specific purpose sales and use tax, the Cityintends to seek support from the voters
in Laramie Countyfor approval and useof taxpayer funds for the relocation and replacement of
several fire stations including in the area of south Cheyenne;
WHEREAS, on July20,2023, the City received an appraisal valuing the estimated market
value of the property located at 503 West College Drive, fee simple, at six hundred thirty-five
thousand dollars ($635,000.00)(See Exhibit A, at p.2);
WHEREAS, Steven and Carol Powers wish to sell their property located at 503 West
College Drive, but they would like to lease the property from the City after the sale while they
locate replacement property in Laramie County;
WHEREAS, the Cityhas offered topurchase the property at503West College Drive in
the amount of six hundred thirty-two thousand six hundred dollars ($632,600.00), which reflect
the appraised value minus two thousand four hundred dollars ($2,400) in property taxes incurred
over the term of the two(2)year lease period; and,
WHEREAS, upon completion of the purchase and sale agreement with the Steven and
Carol Powers, the City intends toenter into a lease agreement with Steven and Carol Powers
permitting them to lease the property from the City in the amount of one dollar ($1.00)per year
for a two (2)year lease period followed by a month-to month lease with a thirty (30) days
termination notice by either party; and,
WHEREAS, the City intends to begin the process of planning and building a fire station at
503West College Drive.
