CITY CONTRACT#
AGREEMENT FOR THE PURCHASE AND SALE OF LANDS
This Agreement for the Purchase and Sale of Lands(Agreement") is made effective as
of the date of execution ("Effective Date") of the last signing party below, and entered into by
and between the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a municipal corporation organized under the laws
of the State of Wyoming, having its principal offices at 2101 O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming 82001 ("City"), and Steven C.Powers and Carol S.Powers,503West College Drive,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001,("Sellers"), and sometimes individually referred to herein as
"Party”and collectively to as"Parties."
WHEREAS, Sellers own real property situated at 503 West College Drive, Laramie
County, Wyoming ("Real Property"), , for a total appraised value of six hundred thirty-two
herein by this reference.
WHEREAS, Sellers desire to sell its Real Property to the City.
WHEREAS, the City wishes to purchase the Real Property.
NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual benefits and obligations set forth in
this Agreement:
1.
Purpose of Agreement.Subject to the terms and conditions set forth in
Paragraphs 2-15: Sellers agrees to sell to the City, and the City agrees to purchase from Sellers
the Real Property identified in Exhibit A, subject to all existing easements, rights of way,
covenants, and restrictions, for a purchase price of six hundred thirty-two thousand six hundred
dollars ($632,600.00), to be paid by City in full at closing.
2.Terms of the Agreement. The Real Property and all improvements, structures,
and fixtures situated on Real Property will be conveyed to the City in an“as is" condition
without any representations or warranties, expressed or implied, relating to Real Property's
physical condition and without ascribing any value to them.
3.Payment of Taxes. Prior to closing, Sellers shall pay, when due and payable, all
property taxes and assessments asserted against the Real Property for Real Property for the
current year and for all prior years.All such taxes for the current year shall be apportioned
between the Parties on a pro rata basis as of the date of closing.
4.Title.
a.Prior to closing, the City shall have the right to obtain a Title Commitment
for Real Property (the “Title Commitment") at the City's sole cost and expense.In the
event the Title Commitment shows that Sellers is not vested with a good, marketable, and
